VPGATHERQD / VGATHERQPS: clear the ymm destination above VL/2 at a zmm index

The q-index d-element gathers return a result half the index width, so the
EVEX handler VGATHERQPS_MASK_VpsVSib (shared by vpgatherqd) has to zero the
destination above 256 bits for a zmm index and above 128 for a ymm index
(SDM: DEST[MAXVL-1:VL/2] := 0). It derived that clear length as `len--`,
which happens to be right for VL256 (2 -> 1 = BX_VL128) but gives 3 for
VL512 — a value BX_CLEAR_AVX_REGZ compares against neither BX_VL256 nor
BX_VL128, so it cleared nothing and bits 256..511 of the ymm destination
kept whatever the register held before. `len >>= 1` is the intended
arithmetic (4 -> 2 = BX_VL256, 2 -> 1 = BX_VL128).

The VEX form (VGATHERQPS_VpsHps) is unaffected: its result never exceeds
xmm and it clears above 128 unconditionally. The d-index and q-element EVEX
gathers produce full-width results and were correct as well.

Found by this crate's differential suite; see docs/backend-differences.md §4j.
Still present on upstream master as of 2026-09-12.

The hunk below is deliberately comment-free, so that this file can be sent
upstream as-is.

--- a/cpu/avx/gather.cc
+++ b/cpu/avx/gather.cc
@@ -334,7 +334,7 @@ void BX_CPP_AttrRegparmN(1) BX_CPU_C::VGATHERQPS_MASK_VpsVSib(bxInstruction_c *i
 
   // ensure correct upper part clearing of the destination register
   if (len == BX_VL128) dest->vmm64u(1) = 0;
-  else len--;
+  else len >>= 1;
 
   BX_WRITE_OPMASK(i->opmask(), 0);
   BX_CLEAR_AVX_REGZ(i->dst(), len);
